    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-032 Commit 1: paint-authoritative `visible` flag on `LayoutBox`, set from ComputedStyle during layout, respected by `paint_box()`.\n\n## What landed\n\n- `LayoutBox::visible` (default true)\n- `layout_element` sets `visible=false` for `visibility:hidden | collapse` or `opacity <= 0.0001`\n- `paint_box()` early-returns on `!box.visible` — single choke point for both root and children\n- 6 tests in `[layout][adr-032]`\n\n## HONEST NEGATIVE RESULT: this does NOT fix ADR-031's overlap\n\nADR-031's leak_locate diagnostic predicted this: all suspicious text fragments were at **y >= 4317** (outside first viewport), so `visibility`/`opacity` culling cannot remove something layout already skipped. Measurement holds.\n\nThe visual overlap at x=324 in the first viewport is **nav-style content leaking** (`HTML5 / HTML and variants / Dynamic HTML / XHTML / Basic / Mobile Profile / HTML elements and attributes / ...`) — not infobox content. It's a navbox or second sidebar variant that `.sidebar{display:none !important}` (ADR-031 workaround) didn't match.\n\nDeferred to a future diagnostic cycle: identify the specific element (probably `.navbox`, `.navbox-styles`, or a `.sidebar` variant with a different class token) and hide it.\n\n## Structural value delivered\n\nIndependent of ADR-031:\n\n1. **Paint is now authoritative about visibility/opacity.** Before this commit, paint drew every box without checking. Now it respects the layout-computed `visible` flag. Closes a defense-in-depth gap.\n2. **Precondition for ADR-033 (`:checked` dropdowns).** 14 `:checked` rules use `visibility:visible` to reveal dropdown content on click. The initial hidden state now paints correctly.\n3. **Sets up the pattern** for future culling: `z-index`, `clip-path`, `position` (once those land) will follow the same \"layout computes, paint respects\" structure.\n\n## v1 limitations documented\n\n- **No opacity blending.** Any `opacity > 0` drawn opaque. Cairo groups / per-draw alpha deferred.\n- **`visibility: visible` doesn't re-enable on hidden ancestor.** Only 1 use in Wikipedia's CSS (skip link, already worked around with `!important`).\n- **`opacity: var(...)` treated as opaque.** No variable resolution for opacity in v1.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 408 / 1692\n- After: **414 / 1710** (+6 / +18)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `visibility: hidden` → visible=false | ✅ |\n| `visibility: visible` → visible=true | ✅ |\n| `opacity: 0` → visible=false | ✅ |\n| `opacity: 0.5` → visible=true (opaque) | ✅ |\n| `opacity: var(...)` → visible=true (unresolved) | ✅ |\n| Default → visible=true | ✅ |\n| **Does NOT fix ADR-031's overlap** | ✅ (documented) |\n| No regression to prior ADRs | ✅ |\n\n## What's next\n\n- **This PR**: merge, ADR-032 Commit 2 (docs) closes ADR-032 with the honest negative result in Implementation section\n- **Next cycle**: identify the actual navbox/sidebar element causing the x=324 leak in the first viewport, add to viewport_css (like `.sidebar`), verify PNG\n- **Then**: ADR-033 (`:checked` + `position` + `:not` + `clip`) — the structural piece ADR-032 was preparing for\n\nRefs #171\n",
